{"title":"Greatest common divisor","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>This video comprehensively explains everything related to the GCD: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HboSeb_gQH8\">https://youtu.be/HboSeb_gQH8</a>\nThe <b>greatest common divisor</b> (<b>GCD</b>, or <b>GCF</b> (<b>greatest common factor</b>)) of two or more <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> is the largest integer that is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisor</a> of all the given numbers.\n</p><p>The GCD is sometimes called the <b>greatest common factor</b> (<b>GCF</b>).\n</p><p>A very useful property of the GCD is that it can be represented as a sum of the given numbers with integer coefficients. From here it immediately follows that the greatest common divisor of several numbers is divisible by any other common divisor of these numbers.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Greatest_Common_Divisor_Video\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Greatest Common Divisor Video</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Finding_the_GCD/GCF_of_two_numbers\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Finding the GCD/GCF of two numbers</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Using_prime_factorization\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Using prime factorization</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Euclidean_algorithm\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Euclidean algorithm</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Using_the_least_common_multiple\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Using the least common multiple</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#The_binary_method\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The binary method</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Greatest_Common_Divisor_Video\">Greatest Common Divisor Video</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_common_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Greatest Common Divisor Video\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HboSeb_gQH8\">https://youtu.be/HboSeb_gQH8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Finding_the_GCD.2FGCF_of_two_numbers\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finding_the_GCD/GCF_of_two_numbers\">Finding the GCD/GCF of two numbers</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_common_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Finding the GCD/GCF of two numbers\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Using_prime_factorization\">Using prime factorization</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_common_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Using prime factorization\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Once the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_factorization\" title=\"Prime factorization\">prime factorizations</a> of the given numbers have been found, the greatest common divisor is the product of all common factors of the numbers.\n</p><p>Example:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f457e82d45a03b06771b0264692e4b2657c49efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270=2\\cdot3^3\\cdot5$\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdeea37183caca35db2f7243c2861657f479558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144=2^4\\cdot3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />. The common factors are 2 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819068968ed60608a91d0c3921d6296964660e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ada395afeb707827e25a7db87aef0e392f17b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GCD(270,144)=2\\cdot3^2=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Euclidean_algorithm\">Euclidean algorithm</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_common_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Euclidean algorithm\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclidean_algorithm\" title=\"Euclidean algorithm\">Euclidean algorithm</a> is much faster and can be used to give the GCD of any two numbers without knowing their prime factorizations. To find the greatest common divisor of more than two numbers, one can use the recursive formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b708456e46c8d9d788f88c4b996d8f005706fd26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GCD(a_1,\\dots,a_n)=GCD(GCD(a_1,\\dots,a_{n-1}),a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"393\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Using_the_least_common_multiple\">Using the least common multiple</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_common_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Using the least common multiple\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The GCD of two numbers can also be found using the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c4f58287c67f58c5335e3503297c2d17ab4024.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GCD(x, y) \\cdot LCM(x, y) = x \\cdot y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"244\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8996e47fed25a7fe672945cab1bf13575b106101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LCM(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Least_common_multiple\" title=\"Least common multiple\">least common multiple</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_binary_method\">The binary method</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_common_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: The binary method\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor#Binary_method\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor#Binary_method</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017130040\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 68/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1664/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1775:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017130040 and revision id 143377. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}